**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.PlannerInputsTests`

**How to implement.** The lab profile is the kit's items; nothing is typed in (001 §M 'Its inputs are the kit; there is no separate "lab profile" to type in: lab profile = the kit's items: sources and lambda ranges, polarizers, compensators, compounds, detectors, angle ranges, and each detector's noise model'; the S14.1 brief, the noise model being the detector parameter axes defined in step 206, with the bench implementation promoted to Optimization in step 339). An item's model is read as the study's forward model reads it, through a `choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option` (`StudyForwardContext.choiceOf`, step 372; the window's `tryItemModelChoice`, step 263), so no second resolution is written. In `MeasurementPlanner.fs`, after step 469's declarations, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.1; every case name has two words; no `bool` appears. (1) `PlannerError` (step 469) gains `UnresolvedPlannerItemErr`, rendered `the item's model is not in the library: <reason>`. (2) `PlannerSource = { item : ItemId; label : ItemLabel; waveLength : WaveLength; tunableLimitsOpt : WaveLengthInterval option }` (the preset's line and limits, `ElementId.fs:SourcePreset`, `tunableLimitsOpt`). (3) `OpticRole` = `PolarizerOptic | CompensatorOptic | CompoundOptic` and `PlannerOptic = { item : ItemId; label : ItemLabel; role : OpticRole }`. (4) `DetectorRecording` = `RecordsIntensity | RecordsMuellerMatrix | RecordsPsiDelta` and `PlannerDetector = { item : ItemId; label : ItemLabel; recording : DetectorRecording; noise : ParameterValues }`. The three unions are derived, never stored, so they carry no wire tag. (5) `LabProfile = { sources : PlannerSource list; optics : PlannerOptic list; detectors : PlannerDetector list }`. `static member ofItems (items : Item list) (choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option) : Result<LabProfile, PlannerError>` reads the items in order (step 216's `ItemModelChoice`, step 208's forms): an item whose `choiceOf` is `None` answers `UnresolvedPlannerItemErr` naming its label, and nothing is answered in part; `SourcePresetChoice (sourceModel, p)` is a source; `PolarizerPresetChoice (polarizerModel, p)` is an optic, `PolarizerOptic` for a `ComputedIdeal` behavior and `CompoundOptic` for a `ConstantMueller` one (`ElementId.fs:PolarizerBehavior`); a `LibraryModelChoice v` reads `v.entry.model`: `OpticalElementModel (RealPolarizerModel _)` is a `PolarizerOptic`, `RetarderPlateModel _` a `CompensatorOptic`, `CompoundModel components` a `CompoundOptic` when a component at any depth is a `RealPolarizerModel` and a `CompensatorOptic` otherwise, `BlackBoxMuellerModel _` and `EmptySlotModel` are neither (an object and the calibration reference), and `IntensityDetectorModel n`, `MuellerPolarimeterModel n` and `EllipsometerModel n` are detectors recording `RecordsIntensity`, `RecordsMuellerMatrix` and `RecordsPsiDelta` with noise ParameterValues.ofParameters of that detector item, checked against n; a missing or invalid noise value MUST answer UnresolvedPlannerItemErr naming the item and the rejected axis; a `StackSampleChoice` is no part of the profile (the plates are read in step 471). `member this.reachOf (detector : PlannerDetector) : DetectorReach`: `FullMuellerReach` for `RecordsMuellerMatrix`, `EllipsometricReach` for `RecordsPsiDelta`, and for `RecordsIntensity` `FullMuellerReach` when the profile holds two or more polarizing optics (`PolarizerOptic` or `CompoundOptic`), a polarizer and an analyzer around the plate (the HAUP class, 001 §M), and `IntensityOnlyReach` otherwise. `member this.reaches : DetectorReach list`: each reach some detector's `reachOf` answers, once, in the order `FullMuellerReach`, `EllipsometricReach`, `IntensityOnlyReach`. No other member is added. Tests: new `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PlannerInputsTests.fs`, `module PlannerInputsTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Its items are made by `ItemDraft.toItem` (step 216) with `FixedMounting`, over the Built-in catalogue as `BuiltinCatalogue` reads it (steps 207, 210): `Laser` (`SourcePresetChoice` of `PresetIds.heNe633`), `LP1` and `LP2` (`PolarizerPresetChoice` of `PresetIds.polarizerLp`), `CPL1` (`ItemModelIds.circularPolarizerModelId`), `RET` (`ItemModelIds.retarderPlateModelId`), `Phone` (`ItemModelIds.intensityDetectorModelId`), `Polarimeter` (`ItemModelIds.muellerPolarimeterModelId`), `Ellipsometer` (`ItemModelIds.ellipsometerModelId`) and `GL` (`StackSampleChoice` of `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1), and a test-local `choiceOf` answers each item's draft model. `the lab profile reads the kit's sources, optics and detectors from their models`: over all nine, `sources` is [Laser] at the preset's `waveLength` with no limits; `optics` is LP1 and LP2 `PolarizerOptic`, CPL1 `CompoundOptic` and RET `CompensatorOptic`, in item order; `detectors` is Phone `RecordsIntensity`, Polarimeter `RecordsMuellerMatrix` and Ellipsometer `RecordsPsiDelta`, each with the noise ParameterValues derived from that item's parameter states; GL is in none. `an intensity detector reaches a full Mueller matrix only between a polarizer and an analyzer`: in a profile of Phone, LP1 and CPL1, `reachOf` Phone is `FullMuellerReach`; of Phone and LP1, or of Phone, LP1 and RET, `IntensityOnlyReach`; Polarimeter's is `FullMuellerReach` and Ellipsometer's `EllipsometricReach` in any profile; and the `reaches` of a profile of Phone, LP1 and Ellipsometer are [EllipsometricReach; IntensityOnlyReach]. `an item whose model the library does not resolve refuses the lab profile, naming it`: a `choiceOf` answering `None` for LP2 makes `ofItems` answer `UnresolvedPlannerItemErr` naming `LP2`, its `describe` starting `the item's model is not in the library: `. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved. The first fact MUST additionally change one detector's rotationUncertainty parameter and verify that its lab-profile noise reads that value rather than the library default. MeasurementPlanner.fs MUST open OpticalConstructor.Domain.ItemEvaluation for ParameterValues; the Domain lab-profile code MUST NOT open or reference Optimization.

**Acceptance.** After the lab profile lands, `LabProfile.ofItems` MUST read every kit item's model into sources, optics and detectors (with their noise models) or refuse an unresolved item, and `reachOf` MUST give an intensity detector a full Mueller reach only beside two polarizing optics; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the lab profile reads the kit's sources, optics and detectors from their models`, `an intensity detector reaches a full Mueller matrix only between a polarizer and an analyzer` and `an item whose model the library does not resolve refuses the lab profile, naming it`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s45 invariants MUST pass.
